any BIOS updates for the QLogic, and don't think that would be a problem.
Sounds like you may have typed in the root wrong during the install.

JJ (the other reply to your post) is right too - get rid of any and all
partitions before installing, even that 6Mb FAT partition. Could be
buggering up the boot loader. BTW, when you partition the disk in
BSD mode (sorry, the graphical install doesn't work, that's why its "boot
dka400 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 expert text"), make sure
you start the partition at cylinder 2 or 3 - you have to leave room for
bootlx.


