Most AT PSUs don't have a 3.3V supply - probably the easiest is to get an
ATX PSU which has 3.3V supply and cut the motherboard plug off and solder on
some AT plugs for the EB164 - you will still need to get hold of some plugs
for the 3.3V connectors which are seperate unless you are brave enough to
solder the wires directly to the motherboard. I have the pinouts for the
EB164 PSU kicking around somewhere...

