The Ultimate workstation 533, is really an AlphaServer 1200 which is a
cousin of the Rawhide 4X00, do not use milo, use SRM and BSD disk labels.
(do you have the 2 cpu's).. you may need to replace the video, most had
Intense 3D tga which is not supported by X

SRM is already on the box.. alphabios->setup->cmos-setup->F6 advanced-> 1/2
down the screen select SRM UNIX->F10->F10->continue->power-cycle

If you have a RH6.1 cd

boot -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 expert text"

when you get to the part to do partitions.. type alt-F2 and get a console
screen
type fdisk  /tmp/sda
type b   (for bsd labels)
follow instructions to create the inital label (or type m for menu)
after you create a label (anything)
type "w" to write it
then type "q"
to exit..

push reset on the system then at the srm prompt ( >>>)
type boot -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0"

follow the instructions, RH will recreate the bds partitions it needs..
after the installation completes...

reboot using  boot dka0 -fl 0   (Assumes dka0 is your first disk to which
you installed.)

JJ
covered this on 3/27/00 in this conf..


