>
> > one. If you have a normal login prompt, you login & start X, and X fails
> > to run, it probably would just go back to the shell where you could try
> > again.
>
> That is, unless the "check cable" message is generated by the
> monitor. Does it look like it's generated by the video card, or is it
> from the monitor (i.e. does it look like text-mode text? if so, it's
> from the video card.)

It is most certainly from the monitor. Usually video cards don't check
if there is anyone using their signal. Moreover, if the video card can
generate such a message, it can also generate everything else, so you
wouldn't see a black screen. On the other hand, the current generation
of monitors produces the above error message if they don't get any signal.
If you have an older monitor without OSD, you will simply see a blank
screen without a message.







