No.. use SRM..

in setup goto cmos setup, F6 for advanced settings 1/2 way down is the
console selection, Select SRM Unix,  F10 to save (follow on screen
instructions)

from SRM to go back to AlphaBios, type "set os_type nt" and power cycle.

The tricky part os to create bsd style disk labels, and if you box has a tga
video card you have to use text mode install.

I boot the CD  (boot dka400 -fi /kernel/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0
expert text"
Get far enough into the setup where a alt-f# will bring up a console and run
fdisk and select bsd style labels.

I just create default labels then restart the install, leaving out the
"expert text" (I have an "Elsa Gloria" which is supported by X on alpha.) if
yours isn't use the same command.

The install will create the correct bsd partitions and install
everything....

when the install completes, to boot the system, depending on your boot
device name. I'm assuming dka0, type   boot dka0 -fl 0  at the console
prompt and you will boot your new system.

This all assumes RH6.1, just notes, not a bible

JJ

