> From MILO I can only do "ls hda1:" Then I can see there is a kernel
> around and a directory lost+found. That's about it. The other
> partitions won't react to ls.

That error message would indicate that you're specifying the wrong root
partition. (I got that error when trying to figure out how to start the
installer program.) Are you sure the hda3 is the root partition? I think
I remember some other discussion of this eror message caused by
something else on this NG.

> With your instruction "cp", how do I get into linux? Or do you mean I
> have to put the drive into my other computer?

You need to be running Linux to do that. (You could probably do that
instead of using the dd command during installation.) Try this:

# mount -t msdos /dev/fd0 /mnt/floppy
# mount -t msdos /dev/hdax /mnt/fat
# cp /mnt/floppy/* /mnt/fat/
# umount /dev/fd0
# umount /dev/hdax

(replace x with the number of the FAT16 partition)
However, this isn't what's causing the first problem. I know this
because I have successfully booted Linux from the hd using a MILO
diskette.

