I use gettimeofday for time measurement.
On my PWS500a with RH 6.1, kernel 2.2.12, this works fine, giving me
microsecond resolution.
A test on UP2000 with SuSE 6.1 and 2.2.13 kernel returns the time with
1ms jumps

The following program outputs 1 or 2 us on PWS/RH and 980 on UP2000/SuSE

could somebody please test this with different configs and help me find
the reason for the difference?

Thanks
Alex

#include <time.h>                               // for gettimeofday
#include <sys/time.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(int argc, char**argv)
{
  struct timeval  tv1, tv2;
  
  gettimeofday(&tv1, NULL);
  do {
    gettimeofday(&tv2, NULL);
  } while (tv1.tv_usec == tv2.tv_usec);

  printf("Difference: %d us\n", tv2.tv_usec - tv1.tv_usec + 
         1000000 * (tv2.tv_sec - tv1.tv_sec));

  return 0;
}



