I have a XL 366. I will try to answer some of your questions.

>- Is there a PDF manual for my system/motherboard?
>- What kind of memory does this beast take?
>- What kind of SCSI controller can I use
>   (or do I even need to upgrade the on board controler?)

You should be able to find some information on
http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/workstations/retired/index.html

>- Can I install IDE drives?

I don't believe IDE is supported in these machines.

>- Can I install video cards other than the TGA card?

Yes, I have a Permedia 2 from 3dlabs. I believe Matrox Millennium II (and
other Matrox cards) works as well. There maybe many others that work as
well.

>   (Should I install another video card... this one does have 16meg?)

Even if you install other cards (say Permedia 2), you will not get
"reliable" 3D support. I don't believe there is stable 3D support for any of
the cards yet (for linux). There is a separate discussion going on in this
newsgroup about 3D support that you may want to checkout. So, what you have
in TGA maybe good enough for 2D.

>- The CPU is on a daughter card.  Can I upgrade the CPU or do I
>    need a whole new daughter card?  If I can upgrade the CPU,
>    which one(s) are supported, and how fast a cpu can it take?
>    If I can only upgrade the daughter card, where do I get those?

For the XLT machines the highest Mhz reached was 366Mhz. I am not aware of a
EV45 400Mhz. And I don't believe EV5 is supported on the XLT machines (I
could be wrong here). EV5 started shipping with 433Mhz systems (au series).
Do check the Compaq workstations page for more information.

Mohan





