Kenneth J. Lund (kenlund@swbell.net) wrote:

: I have installed RedHat 6.1 and Netscape 4.7 for the alpha. What I am
: having problems with is when I use KDE as the desktop.

Well, yes. KDE is, and as far as I can tell, always was really buggy.
Possibly bugs are masked by architecture features of Intel chips but
they hit hard at least on Alpha.  Gnome is also not without faults but
at least does not seem to include real "show stoppers" like KDE which
likes to do something really low-level stupid and to crash my video
hardware.  I observed that in different hardware configurations so this
does not seem to be some particular card specific phenomenon.  After
such crash the only way out not involving a power switch is to logon
over a network and run 'reboot' before things will deteriorate (and they
will pretty soon).

The worst offender is probably kwm (although kdm seems to have also
its share of funnies).  This means that running individual KDE
applications from a Gnome desktop is likely ok most of the time.
Attempts to run KDE desktop on Alpha emulate Windows too well for
my tastes.

If you would like to attempt to debug KDE then more power to you
and have fun with a write-only languague this software was written.
(Before you will try to tell me that this is not supposed to be
"write-only" spent some time, in practice and not in theory,
hunting for bugs in KDE).  Maybe upcoming 2.0 will be in a better
shape.  This remains to be seen.

  Michal




