I went through this recently, and I found plenty. Here's one that I liked
most:

    www.quant-x.com/Software/Linux/Installing.htm

Remember to follow the instructions carefully.  If you plan to keep your
NT4.0 then you will have to decide on
how to partition your disks (I didn't). I used the Workstation Installation
during the install process, and it configured everything
for me on one partition (including /, swap and /usr).

If you plan to do the installation over the net - alphalinux.org has an ftp
site which contains Redhat 6.1 distribution. If you have a
a fast network, then the overall installation takes no more than 1.5 hrs.
More than likely you have a Permedia 2 card (or a Matrox card)
and the RH 6.1 contains 2D support for this (and this should be sufficient
to bring up the server).

If you have a CD, then I expect a faster install cycle.

Hope this helps!!

Mohan






