> In the installation instructions for Alpha are instructions to switch
> to the console2 and copy milo and loadlin to an 2MB partition. I tried
> to, but the recommended command (dd) was not known by bash#.

This is a classic example of bad instructions. Even if it had dd, this
would be a messy way to install MILO. What you should do is mount the
FAT16 partition (if necessary, first mkdosfs it) and copy the files from
the MILO floppy onto it with cp.

> When I look using milo onto my harddrive, I see some partitions, but
> only partition hda1 is connectable. It seems to have a kernel, but I
> cannot boot.
> Obviously I am doing some wrong or there is some information missing. I
> hope somebody will help.
> Configuration:
> Dec AXPpci33
> 2 GB HD (IDE)
> 3x scsi cdrom (id=2)
> 32 MB
> Tsenglabs ET4000a video

It would be helpful to know what boot command you're using (this is what
appears in the "load options" (I think that's what it's called) field in
ARC. Do you know where the root partition is? If not, you should run the
installer again and find out where it is.

Assuming that the root fs is on /dev/hda4, you would probably use:
boot hda1:/vmlinuz root=/dev/hda4

Also, what kind of error messages does it generate?
