Scott,

What you are doing is booting from your CD-ROM dka500:
from kernels/generic.gz and then it tries to load the
root system from root=/dev/sda? 

/dev/sda0 is your DKA0: device. Normally root= will
point at your / root file system, for example, on
my Alpha it points at root=/dev/sda3.

The problem is it is not finding any root system on
/dev/sda? Have you loaded Linux onto any partitions
on /dev/sda? or are you booting for the first time?

If you are booting for the first time then you should
point root= at a valid Linux root file system on your
CD-ROM which should be /dev/scd0. 

Alternatively you could boot from floppy dva0: 
root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 and then install your
system from the CD-ROM (this is sometimes more 
reliable).


alan


