It sounds like you want to build your own Alpha?

I have not done this (although I have been tempted
by the very fast motherboards on offer on eBay).
Some are with and some are with-out a CPU. If you 
can buy one and make it work you'll have a very fast 
machine.

However, the AXP boards usually require a special
power supply. I believe the ATX boxes do not supply
all the voltages. The board will fit but you'll 
have to change the power supply.

Most of the machines I have were purchased from the 
places I worked (some of them were given to me) 
Alpha 200's which are still really nice machines.

If you don't want the very fastest Alpha's you can
buy (as I have done) some really nice Alpha's, such
as the AlphaStation 255/300 quite cheaply on eBay
(this machine is really well built). I have a 450MHz 
machine which I purchased on eBay, and I put an 18.2gig
Seagate SCSI disk in it. There are no problems with
the power supply they ias are all dual 115/220v. And 
they all run Linux just fine.

Pick a dealer who will accept Master Card/Visa and
pay the air-freight, 14-21 days is cheaper (and 17% 
VAT customs duty) it's still cheaper than buying in 
the U.K. (I'm sorry to have to say that).

