Cheers for the info - for those that are interested all that is required is
to tie the pin through which the motherboard tells the PSU to shutdown to 0V
(pin 14 [green wire] to pin 13 [black wire] ). You can do this by hardwiring
the pins together but then you would have to switch the 'puter on/off at the
wall outlet (or better still never switch it off at all :-] ). Alternatively
connect the wires through a case mounted AT type (non-momentary) on/off
switch.

PS this is only neccesary for PC164 mobos like the SX/533 that should be
arriving on my doorstep soon....

