> The missing piece is "thread-local static storage", which requires ld
> support (not the kernel).  In OpenMP. you can designate static storage
> (usually a COMMON block) as thread-local.  Our Tru64 implementation of
> this was to have ld generate the "key" that is used at run-time to
> locate TLS and to cause some initialization code to be called to
> allocate the storage.  There's probably a bit more to it, but that's
> the essence.  Yes, other implementations are possible, but that's the
> one we chose for optimum performance.

Interesting. Yes, that's probably something that works better if you
can modify ld than if you can't modify ld.

