Mohan Vaghul wrote:
> 
> I just installed netscape (obtained from the Compaq linux software web page)
> on my xl 366. On invoking netscape, I get an error:
> 
> Xlib: connection to ":0.0" refused by server
> Xlib: Client is not authorized to connect to Server
> Error: Can't open display: :0
> 
> Any ideas why I am getting this error?
> 
> Mohan

It's the same error you get if you try and display a window
on another machine's xserver without being allowed to by xhost.
So, what I'd try is 'xhost + localhost' and try it again.

Sometimes if you log in as one user and try to run something
as another user (like you logged in as 'bob' and tried run
netscape as 'root'), you'll get this error, too.

xhost will probably fix it, but you have to consider that
xhost is insecure.  Once you xhost + <some machine>, anyone
on that machine can pop up windows on your display and
possibly even run some kind of program that logs all of the
X events (like when you typed your password...).

So, use it with caution and _never_ just 'xhost +', which
allows anyone anywhere to access your display.

Regards,

Tony Hammitt



