How is that going to help?  I think the original poster is asking about how
to change the VGA console mode.  This used to be easy with Intel boxes, you'd
just have a 'vga=blah' line in lilo.conf...

Perhaps you could try passing 'vga=ask' or some such to the kernel in the
boot parameters, I have no idea what it will do on an Alpha but on an Intel
box you would be prompted for which font you want.  I don't know how to do
it on your particular box, but on mine, I'd pass it to milo.

You can change the font with a command like this one:

consolechars -v -M ./ff2 -f /usr/lib/kbd/consolefonts/iso04.f08.psf.gz

but it doesn't change the number of rows of text displayed.

On intel, there's a command called resizecons in the console-tools package
that hasn't been ported to alpha.  This may imply that it's not possible,
but I don't know.

Good luck,

Tony Hammitt



