it is normal to work slow and CPU-intensive for IDE controller
on PC164. this motherboard was designed to use SCSI harddrives
and IDE CD-ROM if you dont have SCSI CD-ROM.
if you dont want to slow down your system then dont use IDE harddrive on it,
because PC164 has simple IDE controller. it does not support
new features like UDMA etc.
you can try also to add support CMD646 in kernel options, but it
won't make a big diference anyway

