Tom Crabtree <gbsci@gbscientific.com> writes:

> I've decided to attempt to load the SRM console, but haven't yet gotten
> it on CD-ROM.  I've read a few threads that warn of only doing a console
> upgrade using floppy disks, anybody have any experience they'd like to
> share?

I don't think that it's any more dangerous to install SRM from a
diskette than from a CD. (In fact, I think that you need to copy it onto
a diskette to install it.) However, SRM is incompatible with some
hardware such as Adaptec SCSI cards and some types of video cards. (I
have a Symbios SCSI card and an ATI Xpert LCD video card with the Rage
LT Pro chipset, and SRM worked fine for me, BTW.) Just make sure that
you have on diskette a copy of a version of ARC/AlphaBIOS that you know
works for your machine and that you know how to use the manual override
to load a firmware image from diskette in case something goes wrong.

