Hmm, I just did this saturday night, and, like you did not get
the partitions in the order mentioned in the docs. I just said,
well, lets try anyway. My partitions ended up as:
    sda1 - 64MB swap
    sda2 - 10MB fat (for MILO) [large, but who cares]
    sda3 - 900+MB for /

rather than the suggested:
    sda1 - 10 MB fat
    sda2 - 900+MB for /
    sda3 - 64 MB swap

Then, in the directions, I did the following substitutions:
    sda1 -> sda2
    sda2 -> sda3
when reading. For example, when setting up the MILO partition,
I used the command "dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda2" rather
than "dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1" as in the instructions.
Similarly, when setting up the boot entry in the arc console,
I pointed it to "...partition(2)" rather than "...partition(1)"
and for the loader arguments (OSLOADOPTIONS), I used:
    boot sda3:/boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda3
rather than:
    boot sda2:/boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda2

It's running just fine now, autoboots when I turn it on. It
does complain that there are problems, but that's because
I left in the floppy boot choice and the floppy disk isn't in the
drive.

martin

