For setting up an initial FAT partition, get arcinst.exe from
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/softpaq/alphant/arcins.zip (55kB).
and unzip it to a floppy. It's a pathetic interface, but it does work.
From the 'Run a program' menu option, you enter a:arcinst.exe, and
then try and figure your way around. It's been a while so please
don't ask me for help. Search for arcinst.exe with your favourite
search engine to get tips.

Oh, and I like it to be a bit bigger than a floppy. You can put
all sorts of interesting stuff on there that you can execute from
the ARC console. Besides linload and (sometime several versions
of) milo, I like to put a copy of my kernel there. And if you have
a larger (not a Multia) system with an Adaptec controller, you can
put the ACU (Adaptec Configuration Utility) on there, and
access it faster than from a floppy.

/Ryan





