ARC doesn't really mind which partition you use. You don't HAVE to
use the first partition like in lesser architectures, or even the
first disk. So
if you (for example) had an array of 9 GB disks and one REALLY OLD
50MB disk at the end of your SCSI chain, you could put your FAT
partition on the last 10MB on that disk, and it would still be ok.

I think though, that it may need to be within 1024 cylinders from the
front of the disk (likely restriction on older systems, thank M$ for
it
ARC is their specification).

Obviously, you just need to remember to do the right swaps from
the instructions.

/Ryan

