Steve Lionel wrote:

> There probably wouldn't be much point in using heavyweight processes
> for this, would there?  The whole idea of parallel processing is to
> improve run-time.

AFAIK, the difference between processes and threads is not so much in
the run time. It's not even creation time, as Linux uses copy-on-write
and therefore doesn't need to duplicate the whole memory. The main
difference is that threads share memory implicitly, while processes need
to us ipc (such as shared memory) explicitly

- Alex



