In article <38c8d402.355967774@news.logica.co.uk>,
Alan.J.Thackray <alant@aethos.co.uk> wrote:
- I would like to try NetBSD, which requires SRM console. The 
- NetBSD website suggests SRM is only available as part
- of a development kit (EBSDK) which can be purchased from
- Digital ( woops Compaq ). 
-
- This part is now obsolete, and the SRM for this machine does not seem
- to be a freely available download from Compaq web site, unlike
- some of the later models.

	Interesting.. I purchased that CD just under a year
ago..  Ah well.

- Firstly, How could I obtain SRM console for this machine ?

	Actually, Compaq made the SRM console software for this
(and other) machines available late last year, after they
announced the discontinuance of NT for the alpha. I received a
piece of mail from Compaq saying the SRM console firmware could
be down-loaded from the following URL:

http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/interim/pc64/

	Interesting, that URL is now DOA.. Oh well, I've
squirreled a copy away at ftp://ftp.cirr.com/pub/alpha/pci64.

- I would appreciate pointers as to the difficulty of adding SRM,
- Will ARC disappear if I add SRM ??  

	Dunno, I wasn't interested in the ARC console firmware..

- Ah yes, and would SRM boot from the Adaptec2940UW,
- or would I need another SCSI adapter ?

	No, SRM will only boot from NCR/Symbios 53C810 and
53C825 SCSI host adapters.  An '810 based adapter can be
purchased from Corporate Systems Center (http://www.corpsys.com)
for about US$40 plus shipping.

- I would be interested in hearing from anyone who has 
- overcome the problem of adding SRM...

	Done it.. Quite successfully running NetBSD on a couple
of these motherboards..  Suggestion: Hook a serial terminal up
to serial port one.  That way, you'll continue to have a useful
console if SRM doesn't like the installed video card (I've used
basic SVGA cards in mine, but generally them using the serial
console..)

