I have exactly the same CDR. I used:

cdrecord -v dev=0,4,0 fs=3m speed=4 6.1-alpha.iso

I'm not sure if the 'fs=3m' is still required, but it can't hurt.
(it's just saying to use a 3MB fifo shared memory segment for caching
data before writing it.  I usually see that this is overkill, the
7502 has its own 2MB buffer.  Previously, with Linux's 4072K maximum
shared memory sgement size, the default fifo size of 4096K would cause
a failure.)

I have had problems using older media that wasn't designed to burn at
4X, but this shouldn't be a problem with recently manufactured media.

Best of luck,

Tony Hammitt


