If the AS200 supports AlphaBIOS and has a jumper on the mainboard that
causes it to load a ROM image from a diskette, you could get two
diskettes, one with an SRM image and the other with an AlphaBIOS image,
set the jumper, load the AlphaBIOS from the diskette, wait until you
get the AlphaBIOS menu, take out the diskette and insert the SRM
diskette, then choose "Upgrade AlphaBIOS" from the menu. It will copy
the SRM firmware into the flash memory. Then, turn off the computer and
put the jumper back in its original setting. (I know that this is a bad
method, but it works.)
