Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.networking,comp.os.linux.alpha

This whole mess gave me quite an agony.  I guess I solved and
understands at least partially why all this trouble exists.

SuSE under their philosophy of "the more the better" installs
all three, proftpd wuftpd and in.ftpd (from nkitb) by default.
/etc/inetd.conf selects in.ftpd by default.
Right after the installation, ftp by users works without a
problem.  Strangely, once I messed up the PAM configuration
by updating one of those packages, it started to give all that
headache.

Proftpd was now considered to have a security problem.
So, I uncommented a line for wuftpd inside /etc/inetd.conf,
blocking the rest.  Still the problem....

Eventually, what I found was that the version of pdksh-5.2.14-?
which SuSE compiled is regarded as a bad shell by the PAM.
And the ftp daemon gets that information from PAM.

When I switched to bash, all of a sudden, it started working.

However, PAM does not complain for requests from in.telnetd
even for pdksh.  Pdksh compiled by RedHat has no problem.

SuSE, is pdksh a second-rate shell program?  I wish to continue
to use pdksh.  All this trouble exists for SuSE for Alpha, BTW.


--
G. Hugh Song




