> I am looking for a possibility to boot alphas (namely alphaserver 400)
> without a VGA over a tty VT100; has anyone done that or does anyone know
> someone who knows something about that?

I installed RH 6.1 on an XP1000 without a display, so there is
a good chance it will work on other systems too.

As somebody else mentioned, be sure to include "console=ttyS0"
in the flags each time you boot.  (If you forget, the error
message that tells you about the problem will go into
a black hole and you will have to guess what happened.)

The other key step is to add
  S0:12345:respawn:/sbin/getty ttyS0 DT9600
to /etc/inittab
Until you do that, your console terminal will appear
to hang when the system finishes initialization.

There is more info in
  /usr/src/linux/Documentation/serial-console.txt
-- 
These are my opinions, not necessarily my employers.



