Are you using SRM, did you ever try to use Alphabios?

First, if the date was not set in MFG, The only way to set it is to be
running linux and run  "hwclock"  type man hwclock for the options, this
will write the correct time/date back into the toy clock.

The "date" command was removed from SRM about a year ago, so there is no way
to set it from the console.

AlphaBios date is stored in a diff format, if you try to set the date under
Alphabios, then switch back to SRM, the date will automatically be
corrupted, usually reading 2048

JJ

