This isn't pretty, but it works:

y=floor(x); is equivalent to y=(double)(int)((x<0)?x-1:x);

It shouldn't require too much time to run on an Alpha, but
avoid this on an Intel box, they have problems with
converting doubles to and from ints and it takes 5 times
as long.

