Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

Someone emailed me and said that the given kludge has problems
with accuracy and overflow, which is kinda obvious once I think
about it.

You obviously have to limit the input range to +/-2^31 and it
would be better to subtract something less than one for the
negative case, so make it:

y = (double)(int)((x<0)?x-0.999999999999:x);

Sorry about the mixup, it was 1am after all...

Tony

